            <ArticleTitle>[A case of Morgagni-Morel-Stewart syndrome with violent headaches predominant in the clinical course treated surgically].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>253-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors present a case of Morgagni-Morel-Stewart syndrome with violent headaches predominant in the clinical course. Surgical removal of hypertrophic frontal bone followed by dura and bone reconstruction was performed. The pains ceased immediately after the operation. The authors discuss surgical treatment especially in cases with high intensity headaches.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
